TEXT 64 144 Left 2 ;1. TWO-POLE ANTI-ALIAS FILTER AND BUFFER
TEXT 1056 144 Left 2 ;2. GAIN STAGE AND ADC DRIVER
TEXT 1056 576 Left 2 ;3. CLOCKED SAMPLE-AND-HOLD PLUS ADC LOAD
TEXT 1776 576 Left 2 ;4. TRACK-ERROR OBSERVER
TEXT 64 184 Left 1 ;Rsrc models source impedance. Raa1/Caa1 and Raa2/Caa2 are two buffered 1.59 MHz poles.
TEXT 64 208 Left 1 ;Together they give about 1.02 MHz bandwidth; Eiso prevents the second pole from loading the first.
TEXT 1056 184 Left 1 ;Egain models 1.6 V/V front-end gain.
TEXT 1056 208 Left 1 ;Rout, Cload, and Rload model the ADC driver plus board/input loading.
TEXT 1056 816 Left 1 ;Clock high closes Ssample so CHOLD tracks afe. Clock low opens it.
TEXT 1056 840 Left 1 ;CHOLD plus CADC set acquisition loading; Rleak models hold-mode droop.
TEXT 1776 816 Left 1 ;Berror measures hold minus afe without loading
TEXT 1776 840 Left 1 ;or changing the signal path.
TEXT 64 928 Left 2 !.param RAA1=1k RAA2=1k CAA1=100p CAA2=100p GAIN=1.6 ROUT=50 CLOAD=50p RSW=25 CHOLD=47p CADC=50p\n.model SAMPLE SW(Ron={RSW} Roff=1G Vt=1.65 Vh=0.1)\n.tran 0 2u 0 2n
TEXT 64 1024 Left 2 ;Educational nominal schematic for mixed_signal_daq_transient.cir. Automation substitutes the braced parameters for statistical samples and light/heavy CADC corners.
TEXT 64 1056 Left 2 ;For AC: Vsig becomes AC 1, Vclk is held at 0 V, and the same analog path is swept from 1 kHz to 100 MHz.
